                <pb facs="1042" n="922" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg922"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.00 Revolutions/257: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dearing</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-02T19:00:00-05:00">July 2, 1931—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:42 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>282. My 280, July 2, noon.<anchor n="28" xml:id="d1010-f1"/> Manifestants
                    gathered at Callao this afternoon to meet Sanchez Cerro, clashed with heavy
                    police and cavalry patrols endeavoring to disperse them, and several persons
                    were killed and many wounded. Government is permitting no communication with
                    Callao and will not permit Sanchez Cerro to land until midnight, when it is
                    rumored it will endeavor to spirit him quietly away under cover of darkness. In
                    Lima mobs are milling around in Plaza San Martin and the Plaza de Armas which
                    police are endeavoring to break up, so far without casualties. Press censorship
                    is absolute. Outlook is for serious trouble tonight or tomorrow. Last minute
                    report is that dynamite bombs are being thrown and many killed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dearing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
